## 4. Outbound AD Bind & Directory Guardrails

### 4.1. Broker → AD authentication

* No bind credentials on disk or in env vars.
* Bind account `svc-ad-broker` credentials are fetched from Vault (AppRole or workload identity) and rotated by Vault on schedule.
* Compromise of the bind account is treated as: **ability to mint identities into every allowlisted group** until revoke paths above are exercised.

### 4.2. Group membership: delta-only

LDAP group wiping occurs when a client issues `MODIFY_REPLACE` on multi-valued `member`.

* Broker code constructs Modify requests using **only** `Add("member", …)` and `Delete("member", …)`.
* `Replace` on `member` is barred by CI lint / static analysis.

### 4.3. Active Directory ACEs (least privilege)

| Scope | Rights |
| --- | --- |
| `OU=DynamicAccounts,OU=AppServices,DC=corp,DC=example,DC=com` | Create/Delete User objects only |
| Explicit pre-approved security groups (static onboarded list — §3.3) | Write Members (`BF9679C0-0DE6-11D0-A285-00AA003049E2`) only |
| Domain root, parent OUs, Tier-0 / AdminSDHolder | **No** rights |

ACEs are **not** managed by the broker. Any expansion of the target group list requires an AD change request so Write Members can be applied (or removed) on the new objects. Broker allowlist and AD ACEs must stay in lockstep.

