## 8. Security Posture & Threat Model

### 8.1. Hardening summary

| Control | Mechanism |
| --- | --- |
| Container surface | Static Go binary on `scratch`, UID `10001`; no shell or package manager. **Mounted CA bundle + reliable time source** required for TLS verify and `accountExpires`. |
| Source integrity | Protected branches; `CODEOWNERS` on allowlist; signed commits |
| Directory containment | Creates limited to quarantine OU |
| Group integrity | `MODIFY_ADD`/`DELETE` only; CI bans `Replace` on `member` |
| Transport | TLS 1.3 to clients; LDAPS (TLS 1.2+, 636) with internal root CA verify to DCs |
| Abuse controls | Per-identity **rate limits and concurrency quotas**; global create circuit breaker on AD error rate |

### 8.2. Threat model (summary)

| Compromise | Blast radius | Primary detection / response |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Pipeline secret (returned password **or** keytab) | That principal + its groups until TTL / ticket end; keytab ≡ password for Kerberos | Short TTL; audit join of caller→account; revoke via disable/delete user; never log `keytab_base64` |
| Broker process / code exec | Mint into all allowlisted groups while bind cred works | Scratch + non-root; spike alerts on `creations_total`; emergency revoke paths |
| Bind credential (`svc-ad-broker`) | Same as broker compromise within ACE scope | Vault rotation; disable bind account; strip OU Create ACE |
| Malicious allowlist PR | Expands who can get which groups | Dual approval; Tier-0 deny list; ACE still limits Write Members |

### 8.3. Residual authentication after expiry

`accountExpires` prevents **new** authentications after the stamp. **Existing Kerberos tickets may remain valid until their own end time.** Expectation for consumers: treat residual ticket lifetime as part of the exposure window; prefer shorter TTLs. If AD policy allows, constrain max ticket lifetime for these principals.

