## 9. Observability & Audit (Observe / Snowflake)

All mint and reap operations emit structured OTel signals (and Prometheus metrics) into Observe / Snowflake for SOC and internal audit.

**Golden signals (ADR-required):**

* `ad_broker_account_creations_total{status, target_group}`
* `ad_broker_accounts_reaped_total`
* `ad_broker_active_accounts_gauge`
* `ad_broker_auth_rejections_total{reason}`
* `ad_broker_operation_duration_seconds{operation}` (create | bind | modify | delete)

Additional metrics belong in the runbook, not this ADR.

### 9.1. Audit event (immutable record of who got what)

Passwords and keytab material **must never** appear in this payload or in trace attributes.

```json
{
  "timestamp": "2026-10-09T11:13:00Z",
  "event_type": "DYNAMIC_ACCOUNT_CREATED",
  "trace_id": "4bf92f3577b34da6a3ce929d0e0e4736",
  "caller": {
    "identity": "spiffe://corp.internal/ns/data-platform/sa/spark-runner",
    "ip_address": "10.240.12.84"
  },
  "directory_record": {
    "sam_account_name": "dyn-svc-7e2a1b9c",
    "distinguished_name": "CN=dyn-svc-7e2a1b9c,OU=DynamicAccounts,OU=AppServices,DC=corp,DC=example,DC=com",
    "assigned_group": "CN=DataLake-ReadAccess,OU=AppGroups,DC=corp,DC=example,DC=com",
